  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership Fund: UK-funded Gender and Social Inclusion Analysis for Kenya and celebration of International Women&apos;s Day 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Two complementary events to celebrate International Women&#x2019;s Day in March 2023 &#x2013; one morning workshop (research dissemination) and one evening event (focus on women in research, science, tech and innovation) held in partnership with the British Chamber of Commerce. 

1. Disseminating results of the UK-Funded GESI Analysis for Kenya and getting feedback from key stakeholders to strengthen the analysis; 

2. Highlighting the UK&#x2019;s commitment to Gender Equality and its work with women and girls across Kenya (opportunity to showcase some of our programmes and bring together UK-funded partners from different sectors); 

3. Stimulating dialogue, partnerships and collective action on Gender Equality in Kenya by bringing together key stakeholders around the focus areas of research, innovation and technology.</narrative>
  </description>
